WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.537
- I mean it's unbelievable to me
to watch my friends get 83 good

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:07.507
comments and one person says
they're fat or they're dumb or

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:10.310
it's stupid and they 
dwell and they dwell on this.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.413
And this is why I keep getting
back to this thought of how do

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.766
you get insular and know
what you're doing for yourself,

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:18.051
for yourself.

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:20.721
You know Ivan Drago, 
right, last scene,

00:00:20.721 --> 00:00:23.824
like he loses and he's like,
he's saying I did this for

00:00:23.824 --> 00:00:25.959
myself not for 
the fucking Premier,

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:27.594
not for the Soviet Union.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:30.330
I was in the ring for 
myself and it's a funny scene.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.531
I was born in Russia.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.111
I love the Rocky movies, I love
America way more than the

00:00:34.111 --> 00:00:37.633
Soviet Union so maybe it sticks 
with me but there's something

00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:40.334
about that scene, right, 
everybody knows Drago for

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:41.875
the famous scene like, 
"I'll break you."

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.210
For me, it was when 
he was in the ring and

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:44.878
was like for myself.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:48.633
("Unstoppable" by This Is Wolff)

00:01:04.197 --> 00:01:08.043
("Future Lost" by FVREWELLMUSIC)

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.837
- [Gary] What I'm worried
about is there's a lot of people

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:11.772
listening right now and saying,

00:01:11.772 --> 00:01:15.075
"Okay, easy for you guys to
say," and what I always tell

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.386
these kids is 
you don't understand

00:01:17.386 --> 00:01:19.146
that's how we got to that place.

00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:20.614
- [Aubrey] Yeah.

00:01:20.614 --> 00:01:21.599
- You know like 
everyone's like,

00:01:21.599 --> 00:01:23.710
"Easy for you. 
Easy for you."

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:27.721
I just, I'm just fascinated
by people's lack of patience.

00:01:29.690 --> 00:01:31.692
And I know we live in a social
media world and everybody's

00:01:31.692 --> 00:01:34.661
gettin' all these things
flashed at them but it's crazy.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.964
I'll never forget 
when I started working

00:01:36.964 --> 00:01:38.382
full time in the liquor store.

00:01:38.382 --> 00:01:41.835
Was 22 and I remember 
saying to myself literally,

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:44.705
literally the first day like
I've been working in the store

00:01:44.705 --> 00:01:46.854
for eight years, since 
I was 14, but this is it.

00:01:46.854 --> 00:01:48.058
I'm done with college.

00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:51.712
I actually worked a little, few
hours I drove home from college

00:01:51.712 --> 00:01:54.281
my last day, but the 
next day was the first day.

00:01:54.281 --> 00:01:55.215
It was so weird.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.884
I hated school my 
whole life and that was it.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.919
I walked into the liquor store

00:01:58.919 --> 00:02:00.387
and I never had to 
go to school again.

00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:01.655
It was like crazy.

00:02:01.655 --> 00:02:03.123
It was the best day of my life.

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.458
And I'll never 
forget I remember saying,

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:08.228
"Okay, I'm not gonna say 
a word for the next decade.

00:02:09.558 --> 00:02:11.398
"I'm not gonna talk to 
my friends," this is real.

00:02:11.398 --> 00:02:12.733
And I did it.

00:02:12.733 --> 00:02:13.727
My high school and 
college friends are

00:02:13.727 --> 00:02:15.502
very weirded out by me.

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:20.273
I like just went in a cocoon and
I just worked every minute and

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:24.011
I didn't even think about 
popping out until I was 32.

00:02:24.011 --> 00:02:28.181
Not a word, not a peep, 
not a party, nothing.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:30.951
And now, I've got 
kids emailing me like,

00:02:30.951 --> 00:02:33.207
"Gary, thank you so much. 
I love your videos.

00:02:33.207 --> 00:02:35.789
"You inspire me 
when I'm super down.

00:02:35.789 --> 00:02:37.791
"I almost gave up last week.

00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:40.230
"Yeah, I've been doing my new
business for about four months

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:41.561
"and I hit a real wall."

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:42.929
I'm like what's the 
fuckin' matter with you?

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.398
(group laughter) 
Four months?

00:02:44.398 --> 00:02:45.532
You didn't hit a wall,

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.868
you haven't even 
gotten out the gate.

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.636
You're not even in the car.

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:51.538
You're still like 
sleepin' in your bed.

00:02:51.538 --> 00:02:55.075
I just really want to push
patience and the long game.

00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.611
All this relationship 
talk you and I've been doing,

00:02:57.611 --> 00:03:00.049
